//- The date-and-time form every "edit a date" popup is made of: the card's
//- Received, Start, Due and End dates, a vote's and a planning poker's end
//- date, and a date custom field. Eight popups drew this same form, letter for
//- letter, in three different files.
//-
//- It takes what it shows as ARGUMENTS rather than reading helpers: a helper
//- inside a template is looked up on that template, not on the one including
//- it, and all eight popups keep their own state and handlers
//- (client/lib/datepicker.js, which they already shared - it was only the
//- markup that was copied). So this template has no code of its own at all;
//- it renders the popup's datePicker state and the buttons. Its events live on
//- this template too: Blaze events do not cross a child-template boundary.
template(name="editDateForm")
  .datepicker-container
    form.edit-date(class="{{#if customFieldControls}}custom-field-date-editor{{/if}}")
      .fields
        .left
          label(for="date") {{_ 'date'}}
          input.js-date-field#date(type="date" name="date" value=showDate autofocus)
        .right
          label(for="time") {{_ 'time'}}
          input.js-time-field#time(type="time" name="time" value=showTime)
        if customFieldControls
          .custom-field-date-copy
            +customFieldCopyButton(value=customFieldCopyValue)
      if error.get
        .warning {{_ error.get}}
      button.primary.wide.left.js-submit-date(type="submit") {{_ 'save'}}
      button.js-delete-date.negate.wide.right.js-delete-date {{_ 'delete'}}
